# CONSULT-63 — Miles 7.2e vs 9.3b API delta map (engine-focused)

Evidence pack treated as given. Headers compared: `miles-7.2e/include/mss.h` (2008) vs `miles-9.3b/include/mss.h` (compiled/run today). Engine usage cross-checked in `Audio.cpp` (`Sound2d.cpp` has **zero** `AIL_*` calls — one comment only).

---

## 1. Stream API

### 1a. `HSTREAM` / `MSTREAM_TYPE` visibility

| Item | 7.2e | 9.3b | Semantic delta |
|------|------|------|----------------|
| Handle typedef | `typedef struct _STREAM FAR* HSTREAM` (5286) | `typedef struct _STREAM* HSTREAM` (4264) | Same opaque handle; `FAR` dropped |
| Struct exposed | Full `MSTREAM_TYPE` (5290–5365) | Full `MSTREAM_TYPE` (4270–4339) | **Layout changed** — not ABI-compatible |
| Buffer ring | `bufs[3]`, triple-buffer indices `buf1/2/3` (5300–5321) | `bufs[MSS_STREAM_CHUNKS]` where `MSS_STREAM_CHUNKS=8` (4268, 4280) | **3 → 8 chunks**; different refill/EOF choreography |
| Async I/O | `void FAR* asyncs[3]` (5305) | `struct MilesAsyncRead asyncs[8]` + `asyncs_loaded[8]` (4286–4287) | Sync callback reads wrapped in Miles async layer |
| EOF/callback fields | `callback`, `docallback`, `alldone` (5355, 5364, 5349) | Same names (4324, 4336, 4318) | Same *names*; delivery path diverges (see 1f) |
| New fields | — | `primeleft`, `was_popped`, `level`/`last_level`/`percent_mult`, `stream_count` (4320, 4331–4334) | `was_popped` forces `SMP_DONE` in `AIL_stream_status` (9.3b SDK `mssstrm.cpp:950–951`) |

### 1b. Core stream functions (signatures)

| API | 7.2e | 9.3b | Delta |
|-----|------|------|-------|
| `AIL_open_stream` | 5368: `(dig, char const FAR*, stream_mem)` | 4342: `(dig, char const*, stream_mem)` | `stream_mem==0` → bufsize = `datarate/3` (7.2e, 3 bufs) vs `datarate/8` (9.3b SDK `mssstrm.cpp:739–742`). Engine passes `streamBufferBytes` default **0** (`Audio.cpp:253,702`) |
| `AIL_close_stream` | 5370 | 4344 | Same |
| `AIL_start_stream` | 5376 | 4350 | 9.3b promotes `autostreaming` 1→2 on start (SDK `mssstrm.cpp:1464–1465`) |
| `AIL_pause_stream` | 5378 | 4352 | Same signature; richer `playcontrol` bit semantics in 9.3b impl |
| `AIL_stream_sample_handle` | 5372 | 4346 | Same |
| `AIL_set_stream_loop_count` | 5382 | 4356 | Header identical; 9.3b sets `stream->loopsleft=count` directly (SDK `mssstrm.cpp:1547`). **`count==0` = infinite loop without `alldone`** |
| `AIL_set_stream_loop_block` | 5384–5386 | 4358–4360 | Same |
| `AIL_register_stream_callback` | 5396 | 4372 | Typedef identical (below); **delivery semantics differ** |
| `AIL_service_stream` | 5374: `(stream, fillup)` | 4348 | Same decl; 9.3b `fillup!=0` waits on async completion (SDK `mssstrm.cpp:1239–1243`). **Engine never calls** |
| `AIL_auto_service_stream` | 5398 | 4374 | 9.3b sets `autostreaming=(onoff)?2:0` (SDK `mssstrm.cpp:1705`). **Engine never calls** |
| `AIL_stream_filled_percent` | — | 4364 | **New** in 9.3b |
| `AIL_stream_ms_position` | 5410–5412 (`S32 FAR*`) | 4386–4388 (`S32*`) | Pointer style only |

### 1c. `AILSTREAMCB` typedef and calling convention

| | 7.2e | 9.3b |
|---|------|------|
| Typedef | 5288: `void (AILCALLBACK FAR* AILSTREAMCB)(HSTREAM stream)` | 4266: `void (AILCALLBACK* AILSTREAMCB)(HSTREAM stream)` |
| Win32 `AILCALLBACK` | 485: `__stdcall` | 471: `__stdcall` |
| Engine callbacks | `endOfSampleStreamCallBack` declared `__stdcall` (`Audio.cpp:349,5382`) | Matches 9.3b `AILCALLBACK` |

**Signature and stdcall: unchanged.** Delta is **when** Miles invokes it, not the typedef.

### 1d. `SMP_*` status values / `AIL_stream_status`

| Flag | 7.2e | 9.3b | Value changed? |
|------|------|------|----------------|
| `SMP_FREE` | 1045 | 679 | `0x0001` — **same** |
| `SMP_DONE` | 1047–1048 | 681–682 | `0x0002` — **same numeric value and comment** |
| `SMP_PLAYING` | 1050 | 684 | `0x0004` — same |
| `SMP_STOPPED` | 1052 | 686 | `0x0008` — same |
| `SMP_PLAYINGBUTRELEASED` | 1054–1055 | 688–689 | `0x0010` — same |

**`AIL_stream_status` return logic (9.3b only, not in header):** SDK `mssstrm.cpp:944–967` returns `SMP_DONE` when `alldone && sample_loaded_len==0` (with buffer-index guards), or `was_popped`. This is **not equivalent** to “stream callback was latched/delivered.”

### 1e. Stream callback delivery mechanism (header + 9.3b SDK — relevant to locked anomaly)

Headers in both versions expose `docallback` (“set when it time to poll for a callback”) at 7.2e:5364, 9.3b:4336, but **9.3b source makes the split explicit**:

1. `docallback=1` is set only inside `load_buffer_into_Miles()` when `alldone==1 && loadedsizes[index]==0`, then `alldone` becomes 2 (SDK `mssstrm.cpp:172–176`).
2. Delivery happens in `background()` timer (registered at first `AIL_open_stream`, **16 Hz** — SDK `mssstrm.cpp:841–851`), only if `autostreaming==2`, `noback==0`, and `AIL_sample_status(samp) != SMP_PLAYING` (SDK `mssstrm.cpp:211–229`).
3. 7.2e-era EOB-driven stream service was **removed** in 9.3b: `//AIL_register_EOB_callback(stream->samp,(AILSAMPLECB)background);` (SDK `mssstrm.cpp:814`).

**Locked anomaly alignment:** `AIL_stream_status()==SMP_DONE` can become true via the `alldone`/empty-pipeline path while the separate `docallback` latch may never be set or delivered. That matches measured behavior: **EOSPOLL fires, EOS callback line never appears**.

### 1f. Periodic service notes

| Mechanism | 7.2e header | 9.3b header | Engine |
|-----------|-------------|-------------|--------|
| `AIL_serve()` | 3243 | 2094 | Called ~every 50ms when sounds playing (`Audio.cpp:5583`) |
| `AIL_MM_PERIOD` pref index | 12 (`DEFAULT_AMP` 5 ms) — 1400–1403 | 0 (`DEFAULT_AMP` 1 ms) — 762–763 | Not set — **stock 9.3b 1 ms mixer period** |
| Stream background timer | Not in header; struct has `autostreaming` | Internal 16 Hz timer per SDK | Not app-visible |
| `AIL_service_stream` / `AIL_auto_service_stream` | 5374, 5398 | 4348, 4374 | **Never called** — relies on Miles internal autostreaming (1→2 on `AIL_start_stream`) |

