## 2. Sample API

### 2a. Allocation / init

| API | 7.2e | 9.3b | Delta |
|-----|------|------|-------|
| `AIL_allocate_sample_handle` | 4607–4608 | 3260–3261 | 9.3b impl **always calls** `AIL_init_sample(S, DIG_F_MONO_16)` inside allocate (SDK `wavefile.cpp:4681`) |
| `AIL_init_sample` | 4687–4688: `(HSAMPLE, S32 format)` | 3550–3551: same | **Signature unchanged.** `format` still `DIG_F_*` code. Engine **never calls directly** |
| `AIL_set_named_sample_file` | 4697–4701 | 3560–3564 | 9.3b impl calls `AIL_init_sample(S, DIG_F_MONO_16)` before ASI setup (SDK `wavefile.cpp:2727`). `block` arg: ADPCM block size / VOC marker flag (`block==-1`); **0 for MP3/WAV-in-memory is correct** |

**Stale pattern check:** Retail-era code that did `allocate → init_sample(custom_format) → set_named_sample_file` is redundant in 9.3b but harmless; engine skips explicit `init_sample`.

### 2b. Volume APIs

| API | 7.2e | 9.3b | In vendored 7.2e? |
|-----|------|------|-------------------|
| `AIL_set_sample_volume_pan` | 4739–4741 | 3700–3702 | Yes both |
| `AIL_set_sample_volume_levels` | 4743–4745 | 3704–3706 | Yes both |
| `AIL_sample_volume_levels` | 4786–4788 | 3771–3773 | Yes both |
| `AIL_set_sample_volume` (scalar) | **Not in 7.2e header** | **Not in 9.3b header** | Engine uses `volume_levels` throughout (`Audio.cpp:3661+`) — **already aligned with both headers** |

**Semantics (both versions):** `volume_levels` = per-channel linear **0.0–1.0** `F32`; `volume_pan` = combined volume + pan. No unit change between headers.

### 2c. Start/stop / EOS callbacks

| API | 7.2e | 9.3b | Delta |
|-----|------|------|-------|
| `AIL_start_sample` | 4727 | 3590 | 9.3b adds `AIL_schedule_start_sample` (3594+) — unused by engine |
| `AIL_register_EOS_callback` | 4912–4914 | 3899–3901 | Same `AILSAMPLECB` typedef (7.2e:2702, 9.3b:1587) |
| `AIL_register_EOB_callback` | 4908–4910 | 3895–3897 | Same decl; **engine does not use EOB** |
| `AIL_register_mix_callback` | — | 3903 | **New in 9.3b** — unused |

**EOS vs stream callback:** Sample `EOS` fires from sample pipeline; stream EOF uses **`AIL_register_stream_callback`** (separate path). 9.3b preload streams reroute through `AIL_register_EOS_callback` broker when stream callback registered (SDK `mssstrm.cpp:1655–1660`). Engine music streams use non-preload 8-chunk path (`stream_mem=0`).

---

## 3. Digital driver + file I/O

### 3a. `AIL_open_digital_driver`

| | 7.2e | 9.3b |
|---|------|------|
| Decl | 4453–4456: `(U32 freq, S32 bits, S32 channel, U32 flags)` | 3139–3142: same |
| Win32 open path | Direct `AIL_open_digital_driver` | **Macro** → `AIL_open_generic_digital_driver(..., RADSS_DSInstallDriver(0,0))` (3073–3074) |
| Legacy waveOut | `AIL_waveOutOpen` commented out (7487–7492) | Not present |
| `DIG_USE_WAVEOUT` pref | Index **15** (1593), default NO | Index **17** (821), default NO |

Engine: `AIL_open_digital_driver(getFrequency(), getBits(), getProviderSpec(...), 0)` (`Audio.cpp:1518`) — correct for 9.3b macro; uses DirectSound backend by default.

### 3b. `DIG_*` preference index renumbering (engine-touching)

| Symbol | 7.2e index : default | 9.3b index : default | Engine usage |
|--------|----------------------|----------------------|--------------|
| `DIG_MIXER_CHANNELS` | 1 : 64 | 3 : 64 | `AIL_get_preference` at init (`Audio.cpp:1511`) — **uses 9.3b symbol** ✓ |
| `DIG_3D_MUTE_AT_MAX` | 46 : **NO** | 11 : **YES** | Engine sets `0` before open (`Audio.cpp:1516`) — **required** on 9.3b |
| `DIG_DS_FRAGMENT_SIZE` | 34 : **8 ms** | 6 : **1 ms** | Stock — drives ring granularity |
| `DIG_DS_FRAGMENT_CNT` | 35 : **96** | 7 : **256** | Stock ring ≈768 ms (7.2e) vs **256 ms** (9.3b) — matches evidence pack |
| `DIG_DS_MIX_FRAGMENT_CNT` | 42 : **8** (≈64 ms @ 8 ms/frag) | 8 : **48** (≈48 ms @ 1 ms/frag) | Engine overrides to 64 in `setLargePreMixBuffer` (`Audio.cpp:5749`) |
| `AIL_MM_PERIOD` | 12 : 5 ms | 0 : 1 ms | Not touched by engine |

**Trap:** Hardcoding 7.2e numeric preference IDs would hit wrong settings. Engine compiles against 9.3b symbols — safe **if** headers match runtime DLL (they do for Win32 9.3b).

### 3c. `AIL_set_file_callbacks` / async

| | 7.2e | 9.3b |
|---|------|------|
| `AIL_set_file_callbacks` | 5445–5448 | 4410–4413 |
| Open typedef | `(MSS_FILE const FAR*, UINTa FAR*)` (5428–5429) | `(MSS_FILE const*, UINTa*)` (4393–4394) |
| `MSS_FILE` | `char` or Mac `FSSpec` struct (5414–5424) | `char` only (4391) |
| `AIL_file_callbacks` getter | — | 4415–4418 **new** |
| Async variant | `AIL_set_file_async_callbacks` under `IS_32` (5460–5464) | Same (4430–4434) |

Engine registers **sync** callbacks only (`Audio.cpp:1507,322–325`). Signatures use `UINTa` + `__stdcall` — matches 9.3b Win32 `AILCALLBACK`. 9.3b streaming layer issues reads through `MilesAsyncRead` internally while still calling the sync read callback from worker context.

**Removed in 9.3b / new:** `DIG_DS_SECONDARY_SIZE` (7.2e:1596), `DIG_DS_SAMPLE_CEILING` (7.2e:1599), `DIG_SERVICE_RATE` DOS-only block (7.2e:1618+).

