---

## 5. Stale 7.2e-era assumptions — ranked by relevance to locked anomaly + storm

### 🔴 1. Stream EOS callback ≡ end of playback (highest — **locked anomaly**)
Engine registers `AIL_register_stream_callback` and historically drove `Sound2d::reset` from it (`Audio.cpp:3558–3560, 5382–5407`). On 9.3b, callback delivery requires a **`docallback` latch** in `load_buffer_into_Miles` plus **16 Hz background timer** delivery when the underlying sample is no longer `SMP_PLAYING` — a **different gate** than `AIL_stream_status()==SMP_DONE`. Measured: poll path fires (`EOSPOLL`), callback never does. Title infinite-loop path correctly skips callback (`loop_count(0)` → no `alldone`); **playlist MP3 tracks register callback but still silent**.

### 🔴 2. `SMP_DONE` poll is a drop-in substitute for callback timing
CONSULT-62 poll path (`Audio.cpp:2497–2537`) reads the same `SMP_DONE` flag but does not restore 7.2e-era release timing relative to mixer/IO teardown. Evidence: prompt 1-frame release **did not change storm** — so the anomaly and storm share a **Miles 9.3b transition/refill window**, not merely slow callback-driven release.

### ⚠️ 3. Stream buffer / mix-ahead defaults are unchanged from retail 7.2a era
7.2e Windows stock: 8 ms fragments × 96 = ~768 ms ring, 64 ms mix-ahead. 9.3b stock: **1 ms × 256 = 256 ms ring, 48 ms mix-ahead** (matches evidence). Engine never re-tuned at driver open except optional `DIG_DS_MIX_FRAGMENT_CNT=64`. Transition anatomy (~16 ms close→open) sits inside a **much shorter 9.3b ring** — different overlap physics when one-shots start (`Audio.cpp:693–697` still documents 7.2-style “one second” intuition, but 9.3b `stream_mem=0` is **datarate/8 per chunk**, not 1 s total).

### ⚠️ 4. App need not call `AIL_service_stream` / `AIL_auto_service_stream`
Headers still expose both. 9.3b depends on internal autostreaming (1→2 on start) and a per-driver stream timer. Worked for looping (`AIL_set_stream_loop_count` per evidence); **does not guarantee stream callback delivery** for finite MP3 EOF.

### ⚠️ 5. `AIL_set_file_callbacks` sync read ≡ 7.2e streaming I/O profile
9.3b opens stream files **per async chunk** (engine comment `Audio.cpp:4517–4520`: many opens, few closes). File callbacks run from Miles IO/async context while main thread batches starts under `AIL_lock`. Different contention signature vs 7.2e triple-buffer model at **track transition ±1 s**.

### ⚠️ 6. `DIG_3D_MUTE_AT_MAX` default is still off
Only true on 7.2e (default NO). 9.3b defaults **YES** — engine correctly forces `0` (`Audio.cpp:1513–1516`). Not storm-related but shows other silent default shifts.

### ✅ Lower relevance (already aligned or non-participants)
- Scalar `AIL_set_sample_volume` — not in either vendored header; engine uses `volume_levels`.
- Explicit `AIL_init_sample` before one-shots — redundant on 9.3b.
- `AIL_register_EOB_callback` — unused; 9.3b removed EOB-driven stream background anyway.
- `Sound2d.cpp` — no Miles calls.

---

## Mechanism summary (no fixes)

The headers preserve **API names and `SMP_DONE=0x0002`**, but 9.3b fundamentally rewired **stream internals** (8-chunk async ring, renumbered `DIG_*` prefs with 1 ms/256-fragment defaults, RADSS driver open, bus-indexed reverb) and **decoupled stream EOF signaling into two paths**: `AIL_stream_status` (observable from main thread — works) vs `AIL_register_stream_callback` (background `docallback` latch — **broken for MP3 music streams per evidence**). The engine’s call ordering (`open → loop_count → register_stream_callback → start`) matches both header contracts; the failure is **9.3b runtime semantics**, not a missing registration call. The crackle storm at music transitions persists even with poll-driven release, placing it in the **overlap between stream teardown/open and one-shot sample starts** under 9.3b’s shorter buffer ring and async stream I/O — not in stale scalar-volume or teardown-latency assumptions already eliminated by the evidence pack.
